{"id": "sllama0206", "pool": "sllama", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.34, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1587, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "Five", "query": "How many senses do humans have? ", "transcript": "How many senses do humans have?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Humans have more than five senses. While we often talk about the classic five—sight, hearing, taste, smell, and touch—there are actually several others! For example, you can sense balance, your body's position, temperature, pain, and even internal sensations like hunger or thirst. Some experts say humans have around 9 to over 20 different senses in total.", "expert_answer": "Humans have **more than five senses**.\n\nThe classic five are **sight, hearing, taste, smell, and touch**, but humans also have senses such as:\n\n- **Balance** / vestibular sense  \n- **Body position** / proprioception  \n- **Temperature** / thermoception  \n- **Pain** / nociception  \n- **Internal body sensations** / interoception, such as hunger, thirst, and heartbeat awareness  \n\nDepending on how they are counted, humans are often said to have **around 9 to over 20 senses**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.07, "stall_ms": 31, "relay_ms": 2486}
